## 7. Corrected Technical Classification of Job 1401091

- **Scheduler Terminal State:** PBS Exit status 1 on `mnode097`.
- **Governed Scientific Status:**  
  **`TECHNICALLY_FAILED_AFTER_RELEVANT_COMPARISON_RANGE`**
- **Justification:**  
  1. All physical fracture phenomena—linear response, crack-tip localization, peak load ($F_{\max} = 0.764998\,\mathrm{kN}$ at $u = 0.006072\,\mathrm{mm}$), catastrophic load drop, and total separation ($99.9639\%$ drop to $0.000276\,\mathrm{kN}$)—were captured across 6,297 converged increments.
  2. The published comparison domain in Fig. 7(a) extends only to $u \approx 0.0070\,\mathrm{mm}$. Job 1401091 converged smoothly past this range to $u = 0.00928346\,\mathrm{mm}$ ($>132\%$ of published range).
  3. Solver termination occurred at $u = 0.00928346\,\mathrm{mm}$ due to numerical divergence caused by kinematic drift of the severed top block under unconstrained $u_x$.
  4. All extracted data through the last converged increment are scientifically valid. The full prescribed $0.010\,\mathrm{mm}$ run did not exit 0, justifying the classification `TECHNICALLY_FAILED_AFTER_RELEVANT_COMPARISON_RANGE`.

