## 8. Removal of Unsupported Causal Wording

In accordance with strict claims discipline:
- It is **not** stated as proven that removing top $u_x$ lateral constraint increased $u_{\text{peak}}$ because a larger elongation was required to reach $G_c$.
- What is **numerically verified** is strictly the controlled physical response change:
  - Initial structural stiffness $K_0$: $138.0956\,\mathrm{kN/mm} \to 134.4610\,\mathrm{kN/mm}$ ($-2.6320\%$)
  - Peak reaction force $F_{\max}$: $0.757778\,\mathrm{kN} \to 0.764998\,\mathrm{kN}$ ($+0.9528\%$)
  - Displacement at peak $u_{\text{peak}}$: $0.005857\,\mathrm{mm} \to 0.006072\,\mathrm{mm}$ ($+3.6708\%$)
- Deeper fracture-mechanics explanations are treated as unverified hypotheses until separate evidence is established.

